e-classic-world-of-darkness/357412-which-are-the-highest-statted-npcs-in-each-game?p=357423#post357423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">number 3 is propably al ashrad. counting each path dot as half he has around 70</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't believe I forgot about him. Yeah, he's a beast, which just shows how badass his sire must be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/357412-which-are-the-highest-statted-npcs-in-each-game?p=357472#post357472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't there some absolutely broken 4th generation vampires in Berlin by Night? Enkidu and Elimelech also suggest themselves as top 10 candidates.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall seeing a rank 6 Garou somewhere, but don't remember any of the specifics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot how crazy that book is, just skimming through it and about every vampire in it is significantly stronger than you'd expect given their age. A bunch of 7th-9th gens embraced in the 20th century running around with 16-24 dots of discipline. There's a Gangrel in there who was kinfolk to the Get of Fenris and has complete control of the local pack, ghouling the five eldest of them! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let's not even mention the crazed Tremere, Heinrich Himmler!<br /> <br /> The actual elders, the 5th and 6th gens native to the city aren't that broken though, especially compared to the youngsters running around. They're superior of course, but not so much so that they should be comfortable in that superiority.<br /> <br /> The 5th generation Tremere Justicar on the other hand is a complete badass, might edge into the top ten of listed characters.<br /> <br /> Same for the 4th generation Seitite Nefertiti who has sired ... several 5th gen Cobra kindred...? WTF? I wonder if you could commit diablerie on them without the negative effects. After all they're not human. Do they even have souls?<br /> <br /> The Ravnos 5th gen Ankla Hotep, is formidable in his own right, but he only becomes broken due to a magic amulent an evil Mummy made that gives him (and only him) full 3rd generation powers in Celerity, Chimerstry, Fortitude, Potence and Protean! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-03-2015, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T07:33:54-08:00","id":358304,"title":"","content":"one of the things i hated in wod was how the writers never followed their own rules. like&quot; square root of your age = your discipline dots for average kindred granted they do say that in the modern nights things are more fast paces but still.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https: